                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "pl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f387bc31-608e-3aaa-bf4f-2404bada2c34",
                        "entry_id": "5b6a45fd-bf59-3937-a5fd-e7a67f8150c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "flaszka"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "augmentative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "54f97743-2ef9-3879-bc0c-5f25f7f915e9",
                        "entry_id": "5b6a45fd-bf59-3937-a5fd-e7a67f8150c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "butelka dużych rozmiarów"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f97ae20-878d-485d-9ff7-0f30f1225bbd",
                                "sense_id": "54f97743-2ef9-3879-bc0c-5f25f7f915e9",
                                "text": "Trzeba było kupić jakąś małą butelkę, a nie taką flachę!"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.2\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "53d1f3ac-24ab-337e-b5e5-d076b9f3f279",
                        "entry_id": "5b6a45fd-bf59-3937-a5fd-e7a67f8150c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "butelka wódki"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "45971757-b2f7-4418-a696-9f20571d3beb",
                                "sense_id": "53d1f3ac-24ab-337e-b5e5-d076b9f3f279",
                                "text": "Zniechęcony jest i rozbity – // Ot, jak wczoraj mrugnął na Stacha, // To Michałek, cholerny prymityw, // Mu odmrugnął i w krzyk: – Co, jest flacha?"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.3\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "71d7d7b3-fa91-3207-ac6f-662c43512be6",
                        "entry_id": "5b6a45fd-bf59-3937-a5fd-e7a67f8150c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "butla"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.4\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5e5d7f48-58a3-4d7a-adf1-bb43c748495c",
                        "source_entry_id": "5b6a45fd-bf59-3937-a5fd-e7a67f8150c3",
                        "source_sense_id": "54f97743-2ef9-3879-bc0c-5f25f7f915e9",
                        "target_lang_word": "carboy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "carboy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dbb462a4-9418-3045-994f-aac4da00aeed",
                                        "entry_id": "b0c49e87-d6e2-309f-9097-626960ae5e27",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large, rigid bottle, originally made of glass and mainly used for fermentation, and now commonly made of plastic and used to store liquids."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b75c756f-86a1-4689-a53a-297da797c7da",
                                                "sense_id": "dbb462a4-9418-3045-994f-aac4da00aeed",
                                                "text": "A few of them then boarded her and were busily engaged in what appeared, from my distant position, as the emptying of the contents of various carboys upon the dead bodies of the sailors and over the decks and works of the vessel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "carboy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2dabe24-a068-372f-8156-2e460ef88f69",
                                        "entry_id": "e811ed85-19e5-3e3e-8101-9377770dee8d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To bottle in a carboy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b13b1d0-97af-4da6-acc7-f3777bf82354",
                                                "sense_id": "e2dabe24-a068-372f-8156-2e460ef88f69",
                                                "text": "Juice bottled or carboyed at this high temperature is difficult to cool rapidly because of the danger of breakage of glass."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dca4bdca-904e-4e02-89df-164ed501cc13",
                        "source_entry_id": "5b6a45fd-bf59-3937-a5fd-e7a67f8150c3",
                        "source_sense_id": "54f97743-2ef9-3879-bc0c-5f25f7f915e9",
                        "target_lang_word": "flagon",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "flagon",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "49fa6f67-3491-37fa-b1fb-9ba6fea35850",
                                        "entry_id": "2260c45d-3ec2-3eb5-a5f4-a34a4a1b7024",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large vessel resembling a jug, usually with a handle, lid, and spout, for serving drinks such as cider or wine at a table; specifically (Christianity), such a vessel used to hold the wine for the ritual of Holy Communion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df2069a5-b0c3-4771-842f-148a56a29562",
                                                "sense_id": "49fa6f67-3491-37fa-b1fb-9ba6fea35850",
                                                "text": "Did they coyn Piss-pots, Bowls, and Flaggons, / Int' Officers of Horse and Dragoons; / And into Pikes and Musqueteers / Stamp Beakers, Cups, and Porringers?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c5372b5-b75a-4a60-b60b-384cbe6f89c5",
                                                "sense_id": "49fa6f67-3491-37fa-b1fb-9ba6fea35850",
                                                "text": "He was naturally a thirsty soul, and was soon tempted to repeat the draught. One taste provoked another, and he reiterated his visits to the flagon so often, that at length his senses were overpowered, his eyes swam in his head, his head gradually declined, and he fell into a deep sleep. […] the flagon—\"Oh ! that flagon ! that wicked flagon !\" thought Rip—\"What excuse shall I make to Dame Van Winkle?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0071504-eecf-4c4d-a15c-cf498f878152",
                                                "sense_id": "49fa6f67-3491-37fa-b1fb-9ba6fea35850",
                                                "text": "Should I ever fill the throne, every Scots lad shall have his flagon in one hand, and the other around his lass's neck, and manhood shall be tried by kisses and bumpers, not by dirks and dourlachs; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bd55440-6ec9-400e-b297-72d6a94674b9",
                                                "sense_id": "49fa6f67-3491-37fa-b1fb-9ba6fea35850",
                                                "text": "\"He's got a venison pastry and a flagon of sack in that cupboard behind him.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6384f4a2-a298-333c-b1ba-62897a3aef2b",
                                        "entry_id": "2260c45d-3ec2-3eb5-a5f4-a34a4a1b7024",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large vessel resembling a jug, usually with a handle, lid, and spout, for serving drinks such as cider or wine at a table; specifically (Christianity), such a vessel used to hold the wine for the ritual of Holy Communion.",
                                            "A flagon and its contents; as much as fills such a vessel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86a1c731-1e0e-4e3c-b4c7-ef355d37b2c7",
                                                "sense_id": "6384f4a2-a298-333c-b1ba-62897a3aef2b",
                                                "text": "A peſtilence on him for a madde rogue, a pourd a flagon of Reniſh on my head once; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb420f95-eb2a-437a-97da-0a0e9d41ecc5",
                                                "sense_id": "6384f4a2-a298-333c-b1ba-62897a3aef2b",
                                                "text": "[H]e had eaten many a meal, drank many a flagon, and uttered many a reproach; […] [Epitaph of Timocreon of Rhodes.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81016a64-291f-31a2-a31a-255171fa4555",
                                        "entry_id": "2260c45d-3ec2-3eb5-a5f4-a34a4a1b7024",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large bottle for drinks such as beer, cider, or wine; also, a bottle with a cap used by travellers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3586deff-abff-4c0f-829e-cfe78498e2fe",
                                                "sense_id": "81016a64-291f-31a2-a31a-255171fa4555",
                                                "text": "[G]o thou in an hermytage of myn here by⸝ and there ſhalt thow bere with the of my wyn in two flagans of ſiluer⸝ they ar of two galons⸝ and alſo two caſt of brede with fatte veneſon bake and deynte foules⸝ […]",
                                                "translation": "[G]o thou in a hermitage of mine here by, and there shalt thou bear with thee of my wine in two flagons of silver, they are of two gallons, and also two cast of bread with fat venison baked and dainty fowls, […]",
                                                "english": "[G]o thou in a hermitage of mine here by, and there shalt thou bear with thee of my wine in two flagons of silver, they are of two gallons, and also two cast of bread with fat venison baked and dainty fowls, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14e07705-9152-4630-98e0-74e96e426133",
                                                "sense_id": "81016a64-291f-31a2-a31a-255171fa4555",
                                                "text": "Bring forth your Flaggons (fill'd with sparkling Wine) / Whereon swolne Bacchvs, crowned with a Vine, / Is grauen, and fill out, / It well bestowing, / To eu'ry Man about, / In Goblets flowing: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "067159be-f3a9-4b74-bae2-596ce6cbb105",
                                                "sense_id": "81016a64-291f-31a2-a31a-255171fa4555",
                                                "text": "They got there bread, and butter, and cheese and apples; the last of the winter store, wrinkled but sound and sweet; and a leather flagon of new-drawn ale, and wooden platters and cups."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aaaf391a-0c02-33af-a2ac-b3e173e883ea",
                                        "entry_id": "2260c45d-3ec2-3eb5-a5f4-a34a4a1b7024",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large bottle for drinks such as beer, cider, or wine; also, a bottle with a cap used by travellers.",
                                            "The amount that such a bottle holds, about 2 pints or 1 litre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f76edefd-58fe-4368-aac0-1fc71a701651",
                                                "sense_id": "aaaf391a-0c02-33af-a2ac-b3e173e883ea",
                                                "text": "Three Jolly Coachmen sat, all in an English tavern,\nThree Jolly Coachmen sat, all in an English tavern,\n And they decided that, and they decided that,\n And they decided that: they'd have another flagon."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
